{%- comment -%}
  YMAL — Inspired By Your Views, source list.

  Fetched as /products/<handle>?view=ymal-ibyv. Returns JSON and nothing else:

    {"handles": ["first-eligible", "second", "third", "fourth"]}

  The FIRST FOUR products of this product's Featured list that would actually
  appear in its YMAL row - the same rule ymal-widget.liquid applies before it
  renders a card:

    - not this product itself
    - available to buy right now
    - ymal.eligible is true (replenishable at Bali To Produce, not fixed stock)
    - no *SALE* marker in the title

  Skipped products do not count toward the four. That is the point of doing it
  here rather than taking featured[0..3]: the web team's rule is "the first 4
  that appear on YMAL", and a stored list's first four often include products
  the row would never show.

  Liquid, not the browser, because only Liquid can read the metafield and the
  live product objects it references.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% layout none %}
{%- liquid
  assign ymal_limit = 4
  assign ymal_count = 0
-%}
{"handles": [
{%- for ymal_item in product.metafields.ymal.featured.value -%}
  {%- liquid
    if ymal_count >= ymal_limit
      break
    endif
    if ymal_item.id == product.id
      continue
    endif
    unless ymal_item.available
      continue
    endunless
    unless ymal_item.metafields.ymal.eligible.value
      continue
    endunless
    if ymal_item.title contains '*SALE*'
      continue
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if ymal_count > 0 -%},{%- endif -%}
  {{- ymal_item.handle | json -}}
  {%- assign ymal_count = ymal_count | plus: 1 -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]}
